hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"226","Wa ʿan ʿAbdillāhi ʿUmar raḍiyallāhu ʿanhumā: anna rajulan saʾala an-Nabiyy ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa-sallam ayyu al-islāmi khayrun, qāla: (tuṭʿimu aṭ-ṭaʿāma, wa taqraʾu as-salāma ʿala man ʿarafata wa man lam taʿrif).. Narrated by Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both): A man asked the Prophet (peace be upon him), \What is the best aspect of Islam?\"" He replied: \""Feeding (others) and greeting with peace (saying 'As-salāmu ʿalaykum') those whom you know and those whom you do not know.\"""""
"227","Wa `alaykum. If one of the People of the Scripture (i.e. Christians and Jews) greets you saying As-Salaamu `alaykum, then say (to him): And upon you . Reference: Al-Bukhari, cf. Al-Asqalani, Fathul-Bari 11/42, Muslim 4/1705."
